branches/C-gate-scaling-determinism.diff:323:+Deterministic BIR scaling family and in-process stage timer. This is test machinery, not a
branches/C-gate-scaling-determinism.diff:324:+compiler stage. `scaled k` has one checked operation and trap branch, one wrapping operation and
branches/C-gate-scaling-determinism.diff:369:+stage's work past the measurement. Returning the result lets the next measured stage consume it. -/
branches/C-gate-scaling-determinism.diff:382:+private def sample (rep k : Nat) (stage : String) (measurement : α × Nat × Nat) : IO Unit :=
branches/C-gate-scaling-determinism.diff:383:+  IO.println s!"sample\t{rep}\t{k}\t{stage}\t{measurement.2.1}\t{measurement.2.2}"
branches/C-gate-scaling-determinism.diff:407:+      | some "quadratic" =>
