+component lean-kernel [kernel] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: - :: the Lean kernel that checks the compiler's proofs :: why: proof checking is the root of the kernel-checked guarantees :: removal: not planned; independent checker replay can reduce reliance on this one implementation
+component axiom-propext [axiom] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: propext :: Lean's propositional extensionality axiom :: why: allowed logical axiom used by the proofs :: removal: remove its uses from the proofs and delete this entry
+component axiom-classical-choice [axiom] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: Classical.choice :: Lean's classical choice axiom :: why: allowed logical axiom used by the proofs :: removal: remove its uses from the proofs and delete this entry
+component axiom-quot-sound [axiom] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: Quot.sound :: Lean's quotient soundness axiom :: why: allowed logical axiom used by the proofs :: removal: remove its uses from the proofs and delete this entry
+component lean-compiler-runtime [Lean compiler/runtime] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: lean :: the Lean compiler, runtime and interpreter executing Concrete via lake env lean --run and the compiled lean binary :: why: the compiler's executable behaviour is produced by Lean code outside its kernel proofs :: removal: not planned; per-compilation certificates attest the emitted output
+component lake [build tool] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: lake, git :: Lake dependency resolution and builds, including the pinned lean-compiler-backend revision :: why: Lake selects and builds the code that the compiler and gates execute :: removal: not planned; replace with another pinned, reproducible dependency and build mechanism
+component lexer [trusted Lean code] slice: slice0 premises: P_lex matches: Concrete.Lex.lex :: the Concrete lexer implementation :: why: its correspondence with the independent byte-level lexing specification is not yet proved :: removal: prove lex_correct and retire P_lex
+component parser [trusted Lean code] slice: slice0 premises: P_parse matches: Concrete.Parse.parse :: the Concrete table-driven parser implementation :: why: its correspondence with the surface grammar's derivation relation is not yet proved :: removal: prove the generic table-parser theorem and retire P_parse
+component llvm-printer [unproved backend] slice: slice0 premises: P_print matches: Concrete.Backend.LLVM.print, Concrete.Backend.LLVM.module :: the unproved BIR-to-LLVM printer in Concrete/Backend/LLVM.lean :: why: no LLVM-IR semantics yet relates the printed text to BIR behaviour :: removal: prove the printer against an LLVM-IR semantics and retire P_print
+component bir-lcb-adapter [not trusted (proved)] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: Concrete.Backend.LCB.Proof.emit_correct :: the BIR-to-LCB adapter in Concrete/Backend/LCB.lean :: why: NOT trusted: emit_correct proves accepted adaptations against LCB's imported source semantics :: removal: not applicable; this entry records the proved boundary, not a trusted component
+component runtime-entry [runtime] slice: slice0 premises: P_rt, P_trap_site matches: Concrete.Backend.Runtime.llvm, Concrete.Backend.Runtime.qbe :: the fixed runtime entry in Concrete/Backend/Runtime.lean that decodes result words and reports trap sites :: why: its native behaviour and exact trap-site output are not yet proved against a libc model :: removal: prove the decoding entry against a libc model and retire P_rt and P_trap_site
+component lcb-lowering-assembler [trusted Lean code] slice: slice0 premises: P_toolchain[lcb] matches: LeanCompilerBackend.Verified.compileFunction, LeanCompilerBackend.Verified.reify, LeanCompilerBackend.AMD64.emitModuleValidated, LeanCompilerBackend.AArch64.emitModuleValidated :: LCB's in-process lowering and assembly rendering :: why: native execution of the adapted function relies on LCB's named trust boundaries :: removal: LCB's preservation proofs for the slice-0 domain retire P_toolchain[lcb]
+component lcb-command [pipeline tool] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: lcb :: the lcb command line that assembles the runtime entry's QBE text :: why: the runtime QBE text is assembled outside the proved BIR-to-LCB adapter path :: removal: emit the runtime through LCB's proved object path, or prove this command's assembly path
+component clang-llvm [toolchain] slice: slice0 premises: P_toolchain[llvm] matches: clang, clang-21 :: clang and LLVM compiling the printed LLVM IR and driving native assembly and linking :: why: native execution of LLVM output relies on the correctness of this toolchain :: removal: not planned; a verified LLVM path could retire P_toolchain[llvm]
+component system-linker [pipeline tool] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: ld, ld64, ld.lld :: the system linker invoked by clang (ld, ld64 or ld.lld) :: why: the linked executable's layout and symbol resolution are not kernel-checked :: removal: not planned; use a verified linker and object path
+component assembler [pipeline tool] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: as :: the assembler, integrated in clang or invoked by clang as as :: why: assembly text is translated to native machine code outside Lean's proofs :: removal: use LCB's verified object emission for every native input
+component libc [OS/libc] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: write, _exit, abort :: libc's write, _exit and abort used by the runtime entry :: why: their native contracts and implementations are outside the Lean model :: removal: replace them with a minimal direct-syscall launcher and prove that launcher
+component os-kernel-loader [OS/libc] slice: slice0 premises: P_launch, P_live matches: - :: the OS kernel and loader that launch images and provide process and file-descriptor behaviour :: why: launch liveness, resource behaviour and trap-line delivery are environmental assumptions :: removal: not planned for a hosted native executable
+component nix-flake [build tool] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: nix :: Nix, the devshell and the pinned flake inputs supplying the toolchain :: why: the development and CI environment determines the programs used by the pipeline :: removal: not planned; another reproducibly pinned environment would replace this entry
+component native-shell-utilities [pipeline tool] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: bash, env, uname :: the shell and small utilities used by the native build helper :: why: they select targets, construct the reduced environment and invoke the native tools :: removal: replace the shell helper with a pinned, attested build driver
+component gate-analysis-tools [gate tool] slice: slice0 premises: - matches: gdb, lldb, llvm-objdump, llvm-size, python3, strace :: gdb, lldb, llvm-objdump, llvm-size, python3 and strace used only by gates :: why: trusted only for the gates' analyses and verdicts, not as compilation-pipeline components :: removal: remove or replace the corresponding gate analyses; these tools are not needed to compile a program
