ISS-0010	2026-11-06	migration	scripts/land/acceptance.sh's check leg ran train.sh check --no-review --no-remote, so an accepted rehearsal (the record the move gate trusts) could rest on a check that skipped review, and agents cannot run it (the permission system treats --no-review as a CI bypass); both its build leg and its broken-build control defaulted to make build, which the restarted root (no Makefile; nix develop --command lake build) does not have; its header described only --no-review and make build. Structural cause: the rehearsal scripted its own exemption from a required leg and copied the old tree's build entry point into two places, so it drifted when the root changed. Fixed on wip/fix-landing-machinery (9b48910f): check --no-remote with the review leg passing on verified notes; one BUILD_CMD default for both build legs; header corrected; a landing_script.sh structural control	R-0563	medium	acceptance.sh runs check without --no-review, both build legs use one default (nix develop --command lake build), and the change is on main	open
ISS-0011	2026-11-06	ci	scripts/review/review.sh's prompts (standard and neutral) made any patch touching what an owner decision covers a finding, with no distinction between choosing a side and recording an answer the owner explicitly gave under docs/decisions.md's recording rule; the review leg refused the facts-decision recording batch, which then landed with check --no-review on a separate manual Codex ACCEPT. Structural cause: the prompt's owner-decision question had no notion of provenance, so a faithful recording had no path through the required review. Fixed on wip/fix-landing-machinery (39059429): recording an approved decision is permitted and the reviewer checks provenance (quoted, dated owner answer or rule), faithful transcription, scope and that nothing unapproved is added; choosing or revising an undecided question is still a finding; docs/REVIEW.md holds the rule, AGENTS.md and docs/LANDING.md link to it	R-0544	medium	both prompts distinguish recording an approved decision from choosing one, docs/REVIEW.md is the single home of the rule, and the change is on main	open
